patch type="fixed" "The CocoaPods specs (`LiveKitClient` and the generated `LiveKitClient-XCFramework`) now declare Swift 6.2 and require LiveKitFFI 0.13.5, whose podspec compiles the FFI bindings in Swift 5 regardless of the app's language mode. Apps built in Swift 6 could previously fail to compile the FFI pod because it inherited the app's language mode. `SoundPlayer` also no longer touches its notification observer token from `deinit`, which Swift 6 rejects for a global-actor-isolated class; a small owner object unregisters the observer instead"
